1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,820
Welcome!

2
00:00:00,970 --> 00:00:03,290
Today we will learn how caffeine works.

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:07,050
Caffeine is a stimulant that helps our bodies work faster.

4
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:10,670
Caffeine blocks a chemical called adenosine.

5
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:14,980
This makes our brains release more dopamine, which gives us energy.

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:19,660
As adenosine is blocked, our brains wake up and become more alert.

7
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:22,800
Our hearts beat faster and we can focus better.

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,960
Caffeine also affects our body temperature, heart rate, and blood pressure.

9
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:30,900
This helps us feel more alert and awake.

10
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,810
To recap, caffeine blocks adenosine, increasing dopamine and boosting energy.

11
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:40,400
This helps our bodies work faster and feel more alert.
